Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:33:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): retain and transport native player permissions

Bedrock 1.26.51 protocol 2193 sends packet 196 as a single unsigned varint permission mask. Native BDS captures confirm camera, movement, lateral movement, sneak, jump, mount, dismount and four directional bits with no position field. Movement disables its child categories even when their individual bits are clear.

Retain each authoritative replacement per connection, filter held auth input immediately, and transport versioned snapshots after joining and late channel registration. Preserve unknown bits. Client prediction and camera input require the registered client integration; mount interactions still need separate native behavior work.
